1	/* Rubik, bundled locally — no network request, which matters because this
2	   surface repaints on every new tab. Variable 300–900 in two subsets: 35KB
3	   latin + 19KB latin-ext, and latin-ext only downloads if a tab title
4	   actually contains one of its codepoints.
5	
6	   font-display: optional is deliberate. `swap` would show system-ui first
7	   and then visibly jump to Rubik — on every single new tab. `optional`
8	   gives the font a ~100ms window and, if it isn't ready, keeps the fallback
9	   for that paint and never swaps. After first load it's disk-cached and
10	   effectively always ready: you get Rubik with zero layout shift.
11	
12	   Rubik is SIL OFL 1.1 — free to bundle and redistribute in the extension.
13	   License ships alongside the woff2s at fonts/Rubik-OFL.txt. */
