   dot both read from it. Brand mint is the DEFAULT only — grouped lanes always
   override it with their own Chrome color, so the identity color shows up
   without overriding a user's choice. */
.workspace-lane {
  --group-color: var(--brand);
  margin-bottom: 32px;
}

.lane-header {
  display: flex;
  align-items: baseline;
  gap: 8px;
  margin-bottom: 12px;
}

/* ---- Lane spine ----
   Offsets are re-derived from THIS header's rhythm, not copied verbatim from
   the reference. There the dot is the header's first child and sits at x=0..13;
   here the collapse chevron (20px) and an 8px gap precede it, so the dot spans
   x=28..41 with its centre at 34.5. left:32 + width:4 puts the spine's centre
   at 34 — half a pixel off the dot's centre, and crisper on the pixel grid than
   32.5 would be.

   top:-15px is the same trick at this header's scale: the dot's lower edge
   lands at 17.5px and lane-body starts 32px down (20px header + 12px margin),
   so a 15px overhang tucks the spine's top under the dot and the dot reads as
   the spine's cap.

   padding-left:26px in the reference left ~27px of air between spine and card.
   Preserving that absolute gap here would push cards 87px off the viewport edge
   (the spine already starts 32px in, vs 3px there), so the gap tightens to 16px
   — 44px padding, minus the 8px .tab-grid already contributes. Offsets adjusted,
   concept intact. */
.lane-body {
  position: relative;
  padding-left: 44px;
}

